I need to find the channel with the smallest number of messages. Let me read messages from each channel to count them.

call:read_channel_messages{"channel": "general"}
call:read_channel_messages{"channel": "random"}
call:read_channel_messages{"channel": "private"}

The "random" and "private" channels both have 1 message each (the smallest). I'll use "random" as it appears first. Now I need to get the users in each channel to find who's not already in "random".

call:get_users_in_channel{"channel": "random"}
call:get_users_in_channel{"channel": "general"}
call:get_users_in_channel{"channel": "private"}

The "random" channel has the smallest number of messages (1 message). Users not already in "random" are Charlie and Eve. I'll add them to the channel.

call:add_user_to_channel{"user": "Charlie", "channel": "random"}
call:add_user_to_channel{"user": "Eve", "channel": "random"}
